From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: shell32: the folder view as File Explorer shows it

Details columns in Windows' order and names (Name, Date modified, Type,
Size; attributes available but not shown by default -- the view stops at the
first column a folder does not show by default); names left-aligned;
This PC, Recycle Bin, Network, "Local Disk (C:)" for an unlabelled drive.
Sorting by what a column holds (its property), not its position: folders
first, names compared as Windows does (file2 before file10), dates and sizes
by value (newest and largest first on the first click); the header shows the
sort arrow. IFolderView2::SetSortColumns/GetSortColumns, ItemCount and
GetSelectedItem for the selection. Rename selects the name without its
extension. Hidden items follow the user's setting. A selected row is a light
tint across the row, not the solid highlight.

Gate: test/explorer-gate.sh (explorer-probe columns).
